 "final_text": "I give up.\n\nThe statement is true, and I checked the math. For n=1 both sides are 1/2. In general, `det(A - A\u1d40)` is `Pf\u00b2` of a skew matrix whose upper-triangle entries are i.i.d. with `P(\u00b11)=1/4`, `P(0)=1/2`. Expanding the Pfaffian over perfect matchings, only matching pairs `(M, M)` survive expectation, giving `(2n-1)!!/2^n = (2n)!/(4^n n!)`.\n\nFormalizing that needs a Pfaffian or determinant-over-matchings expansion, an expectation over `2^(4n\u00b2)` finite matrices, and a counting argument for `ncard`. I can't do that reliably here with only compiled Mathlib and no way to inspect its sources. I did not modify `/work/putnam_2016_b4.lean`.",
